# Domain & Events (RAOS Ch.17–18)

Full docs: `docs/raos/chapter-17-*.md`, `chapter-18-*.md`.

## Domain Model

Core objects: User, Trip, TripDay, TripPlace, Place, Conversation, Workspace, TravelMemory, TravelDNA, Recommendation, DecisionObject, ValidationResult, KnowledgeObject, AgentTask, WeatherSnapshot, Route, Budget, Event.

- One object, one responsibility.
- Conversation does not store Memory; Recommendation stores Place refs only; Validator does not mutate data.
- Include Schema Version + Created/Updated for migration.
- Prefer new domain objects over ad-hoc JSON for new features.

## Event-Driven Architecture

- All state changes publish to Event Bus; subscribers update via State Manager.
- Modules must not directly refresh other UIs.
- Event fields: id, type, timestamp, source, optional target, payload, priority, correlationId, schemaVersion.
- Subscribe narrowly; isolate subscriber failures; support retry/offline queue/replay where needed.
- Event Bus is the only cross-module notification mechanism (target architecture).
